  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, single profile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear +4.2% improvement over the RNA-only baseline (config_001, 0.485 acc). This confirms that adding the image modality with concat fusion is beneficial. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the concat fusion strategy is optimal or whether a weighted fusion could yield further gains. Question tested: config_017 is identical to config_016 except fusion is changed from concat to weighted, providing a clean single-variable A/B comparison. Why best next step: It is the lowest-risk, highest-information experiment—directly exploiting the strongest evidence while isolating the fusion mechanism. The result will inform the fusion choice for all subsequent multimodal experiments (multiprofile, alternative encoders), making it the most efficient use of the next budget slot before branching into larger architectural changes like multiprofile or alternative encoders."
}

